#: pages/templates/facts.html:852 pages/templates/facts.html:862
msgid "Was ist der Klimawandel?"
msgstr "What is climate change?"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:861
msgid "Definition"
msgstr "Definition"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:863
msgid ""
"Der Klimawandel bezeichnet die langfristige Veränderung des globalen Klimas."
" Derzeit erwärmt sich das Klima, vor allem durch den Ausstoß von "
"Treibhausgasen, insbesondere CO₂, die zum Beispiel bei der Verbrennung "
"fossiler Energieträger entstehen."
msgstr ""
"Climate change refers to the long-term shift in the global climate. The "
"climate is currently warming, mainly because of greenhouse gas emissions, "
"especially CO₂, which are released when fossil fuels are burned, for "
"example."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:864
msgid ""
"Dass der Mensch dafür verantwortlich ist, ist wissenschaftlich eindeutig "
"belegt."
msgstr ""
"That humans are responsible for this is firmly established by science."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:865
msgid "Quellen: IPCC Glossar 2022, IPCC Synthesebericht 2023, NASA"
msgstr "Sources: IPCC Glossary 2022, IPCC Synthesis Report 2023, NASA"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:873
msgid "1,5 Grad"
msgstr "1.5 degrees"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:875 pages/templates/facts.html:888
#: pages/templates/facts.html:902
msgid "Klimawandel in Zahlen"
msgstr "Climate change in numbers"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:876
msgid "1,5"
msgstr "1.5"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:878
msgid ""
"So viel wärmer war die Erde 2024 im Schnitt als vor der Industrialisierung. "
"Zum ersten Mal über ein ganzes Jahr."
msgstr ""
"That is how much warmer Earth was on average in 2024 than before "
"industrialization. For the first time over a whole year."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:879
msgid ""
"Hitzewellen, Dürren und Überschwemmungen sind schon heute spürbar. Jedes "
"weitere Zehntelgrad macht sie schlimmer."
msgstr ""
"Heat waves, droughts and floods are already noticeable today. Every further "
"tenth of a degree makes them worse."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:880
msgid "Quelle: WMO, State of the Global Climate 2024"
msgstr "Source: WMO, State of the Global Climate 2024"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:886
msgid "37 Milliarden Tonnen"
msgstr "37 billion tonnes"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:890
msgid "Mrd. t CO₂"
msgstr "bn t CO₂"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:891
msgid ""
"So viel CO₂ setzen wir jedes Jahr durch Kohle, Öl und Gas frei. Über 1.000 "
"Tonnen pro Sekunde."
msgstr ""
"That is how much CO₂ we release every year by burning coal, oil and gas. "
"Over 1,000 tonnes per second."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:892
msgid "CO₂, seit du diese Seite geöffnet hast"
msgstr "of CO₂ since you opened this page"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:894
msgid "Quelle: Global Carbon Budget 2024"
msgstr "Source: Global Carbon Budget 2024"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:900
msgid "3,3 Milliarden Menschen"
msgstr "3.3 billion people"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:903
msgid "3,3"
msgstr "3.3"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:904
msgid "Mrd. Menschen"
msgstr "bn people"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:905
msgid ""
"Leben in Regionen, die besonders anfällig für die Folgen des Klimawandels "
"sind. In diesen Gebieten ist die Sterblichkeit durch Überschwemmungen, "
"Dürren und Stürme 15-mal höher als in schwach betroffenen Regionen."
msgstr ""
"live in regions that are especially vulnerable to the effects of climate "
"change. In these areas, mortality from floods, droughts and storms is 15 "
"times higher than in regions that are little affected."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:909
msgid "Etwa 4 von 10 Menschen weltweit."
msgstr "About 4 in 10 people worldwide."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:910
msgid "Quelle: IPCC Synthesebericht 2023 (3,3 bis 3,6 Milliarden Menschen)"
msgstr "Source: IPCC Synthesis Report 2023 (3.3 to 3.6 billion people)"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:916
msgid "19 Hitzetage"
msgstr "19 hot days"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:918 pages/templates/facts.html:931
msgid "Folgen: Hitze"
msgstr "Consequences: heat"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:920
msgid "Tage pro Jahr"
msgstr "days per year"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:921
msgid ""
"So viele lebensbedrohliche Hitzetage erlebte ein Mensch zwischen 2020 und "
"2024 im Schnitt pro Jahr."
msgstr ""
"That is how many life-threatening hot days a person experienced per year on "
"average between 2020 and 2024."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:922
msgid ""
"16 davon wären ohne den menschengemachten Klimawandel nicht zu erwarten "
"gewesen."
msgstr ""
"16 of them would not have been expected without human-caused climate change."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:923 pages/templates/facts.html:974
msgid "Quelle: Lancet Countdown on Health and Climate Change"
msgstr "Source: Lancet Countdown on Health and Climate Change"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:929
msgid "13,9-mal wahrscheinlicher"
msgstr "13.9 times more likely"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:932
msgid "13,9"
msgstr "13.9"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:933
msgid "mal wahrscheinlicher"
msgstr "times more likely"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:934
msgid ""
"Ein Hitzeereignis, das ohne menschlichen Einfluss alle 50 Jahre aufträte, "
"ist bei 2,7 °C Erwärmung fast 14-mal wahrscheinlicher."
msgstr ""
"A heat event that would occur once every 50 years without human influence is"
" almost 14 times more likely at 2.7 °C of warming."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:935
msgid ""
"Schon bei den heutigen 1,2 °C ist es 4,8-mal wahrscheinlicher, bei 2,0 °C "
"8,6-mal."
msgstr ""
"Even at today's 1.2 °C it is 4.8 times more likely, and at 2.0 °C 8.6 times."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:936
msgid "Quelle: IPCC, Sechster Sachstandsbericht, Arbeitsgruppe I (2021)"
msgstr "Source: IPCC, Sixth Assessment Report, Working Group I (2021)"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:942
msgid "546.000 Hitzetote"
msgstr "546,000 heat deaths"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:944 pages/templates/facts.html:957
msgid "Folgen: Sterblichkeit"
msgstr "Consequences: mortality"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:945
msgid "546.000"
msgstr "546,000"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:946
msgid "Todesfälle pro Jahr"
msgstr "deaths per year"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:947
#, python-format
msgid ""
"So viele Menschen sterben im Schnitt jährlich an den Folgen von Hitze. Seit "
"1990 ist die Zahl um 63 %% gestiegen."
msgstr ""
"That is how many people die from the effects of heat each year on average. "
"Since 1990, the number has risen by 63%%."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:948
#, python-format
msgid "Etwa 37 %% dieser Todesfälle sind dem Klimawandel zuzurechnen."
msgstr "About 37%% of these deaths can be attributed to climate change."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:949
msgid ""
"Quellen: Lancet Countdown on Health and Climate Change, Studie zu "
"hitzebedingter Sterblichkeit"
msgstr ""
"Sources: Lancet Countdown on Health and Climate Change, study on heat-"
"related mortality"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:955
msgid "14,5 Millionen Tote bis 2050"
msgstr "14.5 million deaths by 2050"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:958
msgid "14,5"
msgstr "14.5"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:959
msgid "Mio. Todesfälle"
msgstr "m deaths"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:960
msgid ""
"So viele Todesfälle durch die Folgen des Klimawandels prognostiziert das "
"Weltwirtschaftsforum für 2050."
msgstr ""
"That is how many deaths from the effects of climate change the World "
"Economic Forum projects for 2050."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:961
msgid "Quelle: Weltwirtschaftsforum"
msgstr "Source: World Economic Forum"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:967
msgid "1,09 Billionen US-Dollar"
msgstr "1.09 trillion US dollars"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:969 pages/templates/facts.html:982
msgid "Folgen: Finanzen"
msgstr "Consequences: finances"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:970
msgid "1,09"
msgstr "1.09"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:971
msgid "Bio. US-Dollar"
msgstr "trillion US dollars"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:972
msgid ""
"Schaden durch Hitze im Jahr 2024: 639 Milliarden verlorene Arbeitsstunden "
"weltweit."
msgstr ""
"in damage caused by heat in 2024: 639 billion lost working hours worldwide."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:973
msgid ""
"Dazu kamen 304 Milliarden US-Dollar Schäden durch Extremwetterereignisse, "
"die durch den Klimawandel häufiger und extremer wurden."
msgstr ""
"On top of that came 304 billion US dollars in damage from extreme weather "
"events, which became more frequent and more extreme because of climate "
"change."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:980
msgid "643 Milliarden Euro"
msgstr "643 billion euros"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:984
msgid "Mrd. Euro"
msgstr "bn euros"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:985
msgid ""
"Klimakosten verursachte Deutschland allein 2025 durch seine Emissionen von "
"649 Millionen Tonnen CO₂-Äquivalenten."
msgstr ""
"in climate costs were caused by Germany alone in 2025 through its emissions "
"of 649 million tonnes of CO₂ equivalents."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:986
msgid ""
"Das Umweltbundesamt beziffert eine Tonne CO₂ auf rund 1.000 Euro "
"Klimakosten, mit steigender Tendenz. Getragen werden sie zu einem großen "
"Teil von künftigen Generationen."
msgstr ""
"The German Environment Agency puts the climate costs of one tonne of CO₂ at "
"around 1,000 euros, and rising. A large part of them will be borne by future"
" generations."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:987
msgid "Quellen: Umweltbundesamt (Klimakosten, CO₂-Ausstoß 2025)"
msgstr ""
"Sources: German Environment Agency (climate costs, CO₂ emissions 2025)"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:993
msgid "Ungerechte Verteilung"
msgstr "Unfair distribution"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:995
msgid "Folgen: Gerechtigkeit"
msgstr "Consequences: justice"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:997
#, python-format
msgid "%% der Emissionen"
msgstr "%% of emissions"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:998
#, python-format
msgid ""
"verursachen die reichsten 10 %% der Weltbevölkerung. Die ärmere Hälfte kommt"
" auf nur rund 12 %%."
msgstr ""
"are caused by the richest 10%% of the world's population. The poorer half "
"accounts for only about 12%%."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:1001
#, python-format
msgid "Reichste 10 %%"
msgstr "Richest 10%%"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:1001
msgid "28,7 t CO₂e pro Kopf"
msgstr "28.7 t CO₂e per person"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:1005
msgid "Ärmere Hälfte"
msgstr "Poorer half"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:1005
msgid "1,4 t CO₂e pro Kopf"
msgstr "1.4 t CO₂e per person"

#: pages/templates/facts.html:1009
msgid ""
"Gleichzeitig trifft der Klimawandel ärmere Menschen besonders stark, während"
" sich reiche Menschen besser schützen können."
msgstr ""
"At the same time, climate change hits poorer people especially hard, while "
"wealthy people can protect themselves better."

#: pages/templates/facts.html:1010
msgid ""
"Quellen: Carbon Inequality (Zahlen für 2019), Studie zu ungleicher "
"Klimaerhitzung"
msgstr ""
